    {
      "start_time": 4020,
      "end_time": 4080,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "“Se me rompió el tambor” – Delegación del Este  \nChorus  \nMy drum broke, oh what a shame, oh what pain. I’m looking for an artisan who will put their heart into it.\nVerses  \nI travel all around the island, and I play over there with Wilfredo Morales. The great Kichi turned into a werewolf, and now tell me what I’m supposed to do if my drum breaks.\nI asked Jesús Cepeda if he could help me in that situation. He told me to be patient and to put intention into it without desperation.\nSo I called Papo del Valle, and I also thought of Emmanuel Martínez, who might be able to solve this emergency.\nThen call Víctor Vélez or Rafael Trinidad Maurás. They don’t answer me, and I don’t want to imagine that I won’t be able to play it anymore… my drum is breaking.\nAt that drum gathering the problem was solved, because Alcadio Quiñones put his heart into it, and the drum will sound again."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "tags": [],
      "uuid": "b55a7208-f655-4bba-b386-17e7f17e2cf9"
    },
